KNOWN ISSUES / FOLLOW-UPS

  K1  nilm_disaggregated writeback (P4B):
      Operator policy has no Kafka/MQTT topic mapping for nilm_disaggregated.
      Direct REST PUT/POST insertion paths all rejected by AnyLog (the body
      is parsed as commands, not data). Two clean fixes:
        a) register an MQTT/Kafka topic in operator blockchain policy and
           publish predictions through it
        b) write predictions to a side store (Postgres direct) with a periodic
           sync into AnyLog via the existing path
      Current behaviour: states are returned in /iems/disaggregate response
      and rendered in the UI; persistence is the only thing missing.

  K2  eGauge meter availability (P6C):
      The physical eGauge18646 at egauge18646.egaug.es went RemoteDisconnected
      around 19:43 UTC. This is the user's house network/meter, not the IEMS.
      Pipeline behaves correctly during the outage (last-known data served).

  K3  Remote-GUI deep-link route:
      http://localhost:3001/iems lands on the Client Dashboard rather than the
      IEMS plugin route. Sidebar IEMS link works; final URL is
      http://localhost:3001/dashboard/iems. Cosmetic — the IEMS page itself
      renders correctly when reached via sidebar.
